ExplainQuality:
char *username = argv[1];

This doesn't do any validation with argc to ensure argv[1] exists. 

char command[100] = {0};
char userinfo[100] = {0};

These can result in truncated input if command or userinfo is not guaranteed to be under 100 chars. A loop can be alternatively used if this is not guaranteed.

fgets(userinfo, sizeof(userinfo) - 1, f);

The return value is never checked for error.

There are two else clauses. One of which should be converted to else if.
